  "meta": {
    "name": "Blueprint Draft",
    "personality": "A technical drafting surface \u2014 dot-grid background, cyan hairline rules, drafting-style labels and dimensional annotations. The visual vocabulary is engineering drawings: section callouts, leader lines, revision stamps. Borrows from architectural schematics and Tufte-inflected data displays. Perfect fit for a tool whose substrate IS a call graph and an AST \u2014 the interface looks like the thing it represents. Sharp corners, rigid 4px grid, body sans paired with a technical mono.",
    "optimizes_for": "Conceptual fit with the deterministic AST / call-graph domain, hairline precision, and making the reviewer feel like they're operating a drafting table rather than scrolling a web app.",
    "tradeoff": "The metaphor is heavy \u2014 reviewers who want a transparent tool may find the drafting-drawing language over-committed. Heavy hairline usage means borders and rules must render crisply; low-DPI displays will lose some refinement."
  },
